//===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//
//
// The trailer definitions (ImplementationPlan.md 5.14.4): C-named functions
// whose IL the trailer builder writes (cli::buildTrailer) in an output that
// references the name and defines it nowhere else. Compiled code calls them
// as ordinary undefined functions; llvm/CLI/TrailerDefs.h declares the
// registry. One X-macro:
//
//   CLI_TRAILER_DEF(Id, Name, Return, Params, Scope, Emitter)
//
//   Id       the cli::TrailerDefId enumerator;
//   Name     the C symbol name, which is also the method's name: a toolchain
//            name __msil_<name> (plan 5.14.2 N3), or a standard C name that
//            the trailer overrides only in its Scope (5.14.2 N5); never a
//            compiler runtime helper's name (5.14.2 N1), exit, _exit, _Exit,
//            quick_exit or abort (plan 5.14.4 T3);
//   Return, Params
//            the IL signature as canonical listing v1 text (plan 5.7.10), as
//            in BCLMembers.def: the return type, and the parameter types
//            joined by ", " ("" for none); the method is static and has the
//            default calling convention (cli::getTrailerDefSignature);
//   Scope    a cli::TrailerDefScope enumerator: the outputs in which the
//            trailer defines the name;
//   Emitter  the function that writes the method,
//            void Emitter(cli::TrailerDefContext &), which TrailerDefs.h
//            declares and the feature's file in llvm/lib/CLI defines.
//
// The macro is expanded only when it is defined; the file #undef's it at the
// end. TrailerDefs.h expands the rows into cli::TrailerDefId and the
// emitters' declarations, and llvm/lib/CLI into the registry and
// buildTrailer's dispatch, so a new row needs no other shared file.
//
// Rows are appended at the end of the file, never inserted, reordered,
// renamed or deleted: the order fixes the TrailerDefId values. A row that
// turns out unused stays, with a comment '// unused since M<n>'. Each
// milestone's rows form one block headed '// M<n>: <purpose> (plan 5.<x>)',
// written by the milestone's owner of this file. A column of an existing row
// never changes: a committed definition's name, signature and meaning are
// frozen, and a changed one is a new row with a new name (plan 5.13.7 B1-B3,
// 5.14.4 T10).
//
//===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//

#ifndef CLI_TRAILER_DEF
#define CLI_TRAILER_DEF(Id, Name, Return, Params, Scope, Emitter)
#endif

// M24: the compiler barrier (plan 5.14.4)
// .method assembly static void '__msil_compiler_barrier'() cil managed
// noinlining, whose body is 'ret'. Every single-thread fence,
// atomic_signal_fence and empty asm barrier calls it (decision D36): the JIT
// does not inline the call, so it reloads memory after it, as the barrier
// means.
CLI_TRAILER_DEF(CompilerBarrier, "__msil_compiler_barrier", "void", "", Any,
                emitCompilerBarrier)

#undef CLI_TRAILER_DEF
